  "pubTitle": "Publish with Ember",
  "pubAccountAsk": "Hi! I will guide you to publish **{app}** on Google Play, one step at a time, and I will do the technical parts myself.\n\nFirst question: do you already have a **Google Play Console developer account**?",
  "pubYesHaveIt": "Yes, I have it",
  "pubNoHowTo": "No, how do I create it?",
  "pubAccountHow": "Creating it takes 10 minutes:\n1. Open the sign-up page (button below) with your Google account\n2. Choose **Personal** (or Organization if you have a company)\n3. Pay **25 $ once**: it goes to Google, not to Ember\n4. Verify your identity with a document: Google usually confirms in 1-2 days\n\nWhen your account is active, come back here.",
  "pubNowIHaveIt": "Done, my account is active",
  "pubCreateApp": "Now create the app in Play Console (only the first time):\n1. Press **Open Play Console** below, then **Create app**\n2. App name, default language, type **App**, **Free**\n3. Tick the declarations and press **Create app**\n\nThis app's package name is `{package}`: Google links it automatically on the first upload.",
  "pubDone": "Done",
  "pubConnect": "1. Now I connect Ember to Google Play, so I can upload your apps.\n2. **I do it myself**: I create a special key in your Google account, on this PC.\n3. For that I set up a Google Cloud project, the Play API and the key.\n4. The key is used only to upload apps and stays on your device.",
  "pubDoItEmber": "Do it for me, Ember",
  "pubManual": "I prefer to do it by hand",
  "pubKeyWorking": "Creating the Google Cloud project, enabling the Play API and creating the key (about 1-2 minutes)…",
  "pubInvite": "Key created.\n\nLast connection: the key must be allowed to publish in **your** Play Console.\n1. Press **Open Play Console** below\n2. Copy the address of the page you see (any page) and **paste it here in the chat**\n\nThen the PC browser opens once: sign in with the same Google account and press **Allow**. I send the invitation myself.",
  "pubInviteBadLink": "That link does not contain the Play Console account number. Open play.google.com/console and paste the address of that page.",
  "pubInviteWorking": "Inviting the key into your Play Console… if the PC browser opens, sign in and press Allow.",
  "pubInviteManual": "I could not send the invitation automatically, so let's do it together (2 minutes):\n1. **Open Play Console**, then **Users and permissions** and **Invite new users**\n2. Paste this email: `{email}`\n3. **Account permissions**: tick releases, store presence, app content and orders\n4. Press **Invite user**, then **Done** here",
  "pubGraphics": "Connected to Google Play.\n\nFor the store page Google wants the **512×512 icon**, the **1024×500 banner** and at least **2 screenshots**. If you haven't done them yet, go back to the app screen: in **App logo** and **Play Store screenshots** Ember makes them in one tap. I upload them automatically together with the app.",
  "pubContinue": "Continue",
  "pubBackToApp": "Back to the app",
  "pubUpload": "Now the store page and the upload: I write title, descriptions and privacy policy, prepare the answers for Google's forms, then upload the signed AAB with icon, banner and screenshots.\n\nFirst generate the **AAB** from the app screen if you haven't yet.",
  "pubPrepareUpload": "Prepare and upload",
  "pubFinish": "1. Your app is on Google Play. A few forms are left: open **Play Console**.\n2. Confirm by hand **Data safety**, **Content rating**, **Target audience**, **Ads** and **App access**.\n3. Copy the answers from the last screen: they are ready.\n4. If your personal account is new, run a **closed test with 12 testers for 14 days** before going public.\n5. Any doubt? Ask me here below.",
  "pubReviewAnswers": "See the ready answers",
  "pubPasteLink": "Paste the Play Console link here…",
